p.data['notes']=r'''**Document (134-2.149.note.document).** This continuation sheet bears author page 4 and archive foliation 149. It begins with the visible fragment pé and ends with “avec les”. No date, salutation, signature or closing appears. The readers did not consult another page to complete either boundary.

**Strict Gr-categories (134-2.149.claim.strictification).** The author refers to Mme Sinh’s book and a chapter on “Gr-catégories strictes”, qualifying the reference with “je pense”. He describes the associativity, unit and inverse isomorphisms as identities in the strict case. He invokes the claim that tte Gr-cat. is Gr-équivalente to a strict Gr-catégorie and describes an algebraic calculus with strict Gr-catégories through a “calcul des fractions”, “à droite ou à gauche, au choix”, compared with the construction of derived categories. These are the claims written on the sheet; no external source, strictification proof or localization construction was checked.

**Structure in groups (134-2.149.claim.structure).** The page describes a groupe in (1-ct.) in terms of a 1-catégorie in (Gr). It introduces the quadruplet (L₁,L₀,d,Θ), a group map d from L₁ to L₀ and an action map Θ from L₀ to underlined Aut with gr subscript, applied to L₁. The final line begins to name further conditions but stops at “avec les”; no conditions were supplied from mathematical expectations or another sheet.

**Mathematics and ink (134-2.149.note.readings).** Both capital X’s, the multiplication point and the exponent −1 in the inverse expression were independently inspected. The relation’s upper stroke is bowed above a shorter straight lower bar; simeq is favoured, but an uneven equals remains possible. R3 resolved it to simeq while r1 and r2 retained the alternative; the main crop decision keeps the doubt. Both live barred oval symbols were inspected independently: capital Theta is favoured, with the recurring case doubt marked first in the quadruplet. The cancelled oval after the final L₀ has certain deletion state and uncertain Θ/θ/0 content. The lower indices, arrows, d label and underlined Aut with gr were checked by all readers. No mathematical expectation was used to replace ink.

**Other decisions and limits.** C’s tte and aboutit doubts are resolved; the small interlinear où and the compressed réduit remain uncertain. The word after p.ex. is comment, the group-object noun is singular groupe, the abbreviation is ct., and hom has no terminal point. The quotation marks are paired raised strokes. The first strictes carries one wavy underline, the second one nearly straight underline; H’s note assigns the wave to the wrong occurrence. A low point before quadruplet and a raised paired point after the first diagram target are retained with low confidence. Their intentional status remains unresolved, and the raised placement is not an assertion that the mark is an exponent. No targeted proof check, independent re-proof, computation or formal certificate was performed.'''
